commit:
  - a77bbbf  # chore(#studio): clear pre-existing typecheck drift — 10 errors → 0
learnings:
  - 'Parameter properties (constructor(private foo)) silently create class fields that trip TS6138 if they are only used as the local constructor parameter via closure capture. When opts is referenced in event handlers attached during construction, the handlers capture the local param, not this.opts — so the field is dead state. Dropping `private` is the right fix.'
  - 'TS does not preserve discriminant narrowing across function-call boundaries because the source object could be mutated before the callback runs. When narrowing a discriminated-union property in an if-block that then schedules a callback (this.addSection(label, () => {...})), capture the narrowed value as a const before the call: `if (x.type === "path") { const pathShape = x; this.addSection(..., () => pathShape.points ); }`.'
  - 'Casts like `as AtelierDocument` in test fixtures suppress legitimate missing-field errors. Future schema additions will pass tests silently while shipping broken code. Always prefer proper object literals over casts — let the compiler enforce the shape.'
  - 'Write-only class state (private field assigned but never read) is dead code. If "cleanup intent" was the rationale, verify the dispose path actually exists before keeping the field. If not, drop it — the instantiation side-effect (DOM append) still runs.'
